snapsos/glyphs/README.md
----------------------

20. Lines 222–223: "12 equispaced rotations (every 30°)".
    Code in `geometry.py` uses 12 rotations at 15° steps
    (0°, 15°, 30°, ..., 165°). Δ = 15°, not 30°.
    (Already fixed in docs/dev/glyphs.md.)

21. Lines 33–35: Keybinding table says SUPER+SHIFT+G for
    record mode. The mango keybindings use SUPER+SHIFT+J
    for swap workspace, and SUPER+G for glyphs (normal mode).
    Verify actual keybind in binds.conf; earlier analysis
    found SUPER+SHIFT+G conflicts with glyphs record.

22. Line 353: "60+ predefined glyphs" — actual count in
    glyphs-data/ is 71. Underselling, but not wrong per se.

